1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,100
The first stage of Cadillacs and Dinosaurs.

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:05,913
This time, fight through the hero's eyes.
Revolver in hand,

3
00:00:05,962 --> 00:00:08,925
a big enemy charges straight at me. I fire
several shots.

4
00:00:09,650 --> 00:00:13,225
I took this stage from Capcom's 1993 game
and made an unofficial 3D remake.

5
00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:16,412
Side view is the default, like the original
arcade game.

6
00:00:16,675 --> 00:00:20,463
Vice threatens us, then jumps away. His men
close in.

7
00:00:21,650 --> 00:00:25,438
Press C, and the camera moves behind the
hero. This is the rear view.

8
00:00:25,862 --> 00:00:29,487
W moves forward in this build. Enemies
approach from ahead.

9
00:00:29,538 --> 00:00:32,350
Who enters punching range first? It is easy
to see.

10
00:00:32,775 --> 00:00:36,950
The trade-off: I cannot see behind me. Look:
someone comes up from behind.

11
00:00:37,050 --> 00:00:38,538
I notice only after getting hit.

12
00:00:39,250 --> 00:00:42,988
Press C again: first person. My fists are
right in front of me.

13
00:00:43,213 --> 00:00:48,200
So are the enemies' faces. One last kick
opens the stairwell door.

14
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:51,700
Inside the building, the rear view gives the
hall depth.

15
00:00:51,950 --> 00:00:56,175
But enemies suddenly emerge from doors.
Three of them pin me beside the doorway.

16
00:00:56,412 --> 00:00:59,625
I cannot see the one behind me. The health
bar drops to zero.

17
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:02,962
This build has unlimited lives by default. I
respawn on the spot,

18
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:05,438
knocking nearby enemies down.

19
00:01:06,050 --> 00:01:10,813
Back to first person in the hall. Blade
approaches with a knife.

20
00:01:11,050 --> 00:01:14,338
The blade is waving right in front of me.
Defeat him and a revolver drops:

21
00:01:14,575 --> 00:01:18,075
the gun from the opening shots. When the big
enemies crowd together,

22
00:01:18,262 --> 00:01:19,800
bellies fill the screen.

23
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:25,350
Break through the window, and jump onto 47th
Street. At the end of the route,

24
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:30,725
Vice holds a chained dinosaur right in front
of us. He cracks the whip.

25
00:01:30,950 --> 00:01:35,838
The dinosaur turns orange and goes berserk.
In the rear-view boss fight,

26
00:01:35,975 --> 00:01:41,300
Vice and the dinosaur are both ahead. I can
see who charges first. Of course,

27
00:01:41,625 --> 00:01:43,750
seeing it does not mean dodging it.

28
00:01:44,950 --> 00:01:50,025
Switch to first person, and the teeth fill
my view. A little closer,

29
00:01:50,238 --> 00:01:53,725
and the camera enters the dinosaur's mouth.
That is a bug

30
00:01:53,863 --> 00:01:57,650
recorded in this early build. Vice calls for
help as his health drops.

31
00:01:57,863 --> 00:02:02,650
That punch lands, and I go down again. I
finish by returning to side view.

32
00:02:03,075 --> 00:02:07,275
Now I can see enemies on both sides. When to
kick and which way to dodge

33
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:10,975
are easier to judge. There is a reason the
original used this view.

34
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:16,362
A few final hits, and Vice finally falls.
The health bonus is counted.

35
00:02:16,538 --> 00:02:22,038
Stage one cleared. A score of 122,400.
Mustapha went down three times.

36
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:26,788
Unlimited lives kept this run going. The
footage caught another problem:

37
00:02:27,050 --> 00:02:30,213
fight close to a wall in rear view, and the
camera enters the brickwork.

38
00:02:30,638 --> 00:02:35,145
Those two camera problems were the next
fixes at the time. Side view shows more.

39
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:39,258
Rear view feels more direct. First person
puts you in the fight.

40
00:02:39,712 --> 00:02:43,858
This was recorded on October fifth. The
current demo is linked below.

41
00:02:43,975 --> 00:02:45,870
Which view would you choose?
